# Cursor SDK (Engineering Agent)

Cursor SDK sits in the **engineering layer**, not the student-facing runtime. Use it to build, refactor, and maintain ClearHead — not to power the support navigator.

## When to check docs

When adding or changing how Cursor SDK is used (new agents, subagents, CI scripts, MCP wiring), skim the latest docs/changelog before implementing new patterns:

- TypeScript SDK: https://cursor.com/docs/api/sdk/typescript
- Use the `cursor-sdk` skill in this workspace for runtime choice, auth, streaming, and MCP patterns

You do not need to re-read everything for small edits. For **new patterns** (local vs cloud runtime, subagents, webhooks, sandboxing), verify current behaviour first.

## Boundaries

- Cursor SDK → code generation, refactors, CI, maintenance automation
- Manus API → student support workflow at runtime (see `manus-api.mdc`)

Do not route student support checks or signposting through Cursor SDK.
